  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe downward bias when recent history shows a downtrend followed by a sharp reversal; forecasts consistently under-predict the magnitude of subsequent rallies.",
    "Forecasts display significant lag in reacting to sentiment spikes (0.20-0.40); positive sentiment shifts are not fully incorporated into the trajectory until after the price has already surged.",
    "Model fails to capture mean reversion dynamics, assuming linear growth while true outcomes show high volatility and frequent pullbacks even during bullish phases.",
    "In periods of elevated sentiment, the model underestimates the speed of upward moves, resulting in a systematic shortfall of 5-10 EUR over the 30-day horizon.",
    "When recent history ends with a local low (e.g., <85 EUR) and sentiment turns positive, the model's flat or slowly rising forecast misses the explosive recovery seen in true outcomes."
  ]
}
